docs {
  Happy-path Bruno collection for reals-backend local development.

  Run with the `local` environment and execute requests in sequence.
  The first request generates fresh user UUIDs and a future meeting timestamp.

  Local auth uses the X-Dev-User-Id header provided by DevAutoAuthFilter.
  Firebase auth smoke tests live in `05 Firebase Auth`. They sign in against
  Firebase REST and store `firebase_id_token` for backend requests.
}
